# Snow Way: ski resort snow forecasts (full data)

> Every North American ski resort Snow Way tracks, ranked by snow forecast (international resorts follow, ranked separately) over the next 7 days (<%= Resort.forecast_window.first.strftime("%b %-d") %> to <%= Resort.forecast_window.last.strftime("%b %-d, %Y") %>). Headline totals are for each resort's mid-mountain elevation (summit totals in parentheses), sourced from Open-Meteo and refreshed every 6 hours. Source: https://snowway.app
<% @summaries.each_with_index do |summary, i| %>
<% resort = summary.resort %>

## <%= i + 1 %>. <%= resort.name %> (<%= resort.location %>)

URL: https://snowway.app/resorts/<%= resort.slug %>
7-day forecast: <%= summary.total %>" mid-mountain (<%= summary.summit_total %>" summit)<%= summary.recent > 0 ? " · Last 48 hours: #{summary.recent}\"" : "" %>
Summit <%= resort.elevation_summit %> ft · Base <%= resort.elevation_base %> ft · Nearest airport: <%= resort.airport_name %> (<%= resort.nearest_airport_code %>)<%= resort.pass_label ? " · Pass: #{resort.pass_label}" : "" %><%= resort.snowiest_months.any? ? " · Snowiest months: #{resort.snowiest_months.map { |m, _| Date::MONTHNAMES[m] }.join(", ")}" : "" %>

<%= summary.answer %>
<% if summary.forecasts.any? %>
Daily: <%= summary.forecasts.map { |f| "#{f.forecast_date.strftime("%a %b %-d")} #{f.snowfall_inches.to_f.round(1)}\"" }.join(" · ") %>
<% end %>
<% summary.faqs.first(3).each do |faq| %>

Q: <%= faq[:question] %>
A: <%= faq[:answer] %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

# Snow Way guides

Evergreen ski and snowboard guides by Justin McKelvey (former snowboard shop owner). Each entry: URL, summary, and the guide's FAQ.
<% @guides.each do |g| %>

## <%= g[:title] %>

URL: https://snowway.app/guides/<%= g[:slug] %>
<%= g[:description] %>
<% g[:faqs].each do |faq| %>

Q: <%= faq[:question] %>
A: <%= strip_tags(faq[:answer].to_s).squish %>
<% end %>
<% end %>

# Getting to the ski resorts

Drive times (OpenStreetMap routing, no traffic or snow), shuttles, buses, trains and winter driving rules. Every fact is sourced on the page.
<% RoutePage.all.each do |p| %><% d = p.drive %>
- <%= p.title %>: https://snowway.app/getting-there/<%= p.slug %><%= d ? " (about #{d["miles"]} miles, #{(d["minutes"] / 60.0).round(1)} hours by car from #{p.origin["airport"]}; via #{p.via})" : "" %>
<% end %>

# Best places to ski by month

Ranked by snow days (days with 1"+ of new snow, 10 seasons of history).
<% SkiMonth.all.each do |m| %><% top = m.ranked.first(3) %>
- <%= m.name %>: https://snowway.app/best-places-to-ski-in-<%= m.slug %> (top: <%= top.map { |r, o| "#{r.name} #{m.powder_days(o)} of #{m.days} days" }.join(", ") %>)
<% end %>

# Winter trips
<% WinterTown.all.each do |t| %>
- <%= t.title %>: https://snowway.app<%= t.path %> (<%= t.activities.map { |a| a["where"] }.compact.uniq.first(6).join(", ") %>)
<% end %><% { "winter_vacations" => "Best winter vacations in the US", "ski_towns" => "Best ski towns in the US", "beginner_resorts" => "Best ski resorts for beginners", "hot_springs" => "Hot springs in Colorado" }.each do |key, label| %><% items = TravelList.list(key) %><% next if items.empty? %>
- <%= label %>: https://snowway.app<%= TravelList::PAGES[key] %> (<%= items.first(8).map { |i| i["name"] || i["resort_name"] || Resort.find_by(slug: i["slug"])&.name || i["slug"] }.join(", ") %>)
<% end %>
